From 101d071557304b64fd5f620eb5955617b997aa65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nat-As <42288915+Nat-As@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:29:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] render: bind the Wayland display to EGL for
 EGL_WL_bind_wayland_display

The Vivante (i.MX) EGL driver presents client buffers only through its
own wl_viv protocol, which the compositor provides by calling
eglBindWaylandDisplayWL(); it has no linux-dmabuf client support.
wlroots dropped that call, so every OpenGL ES client segfaults on its
first EGL call.

- egl: load eglBind/UnbindWaylandDisplayWL and eglQueryWaylandBufferWL,
  unbind on destroy, create EGL images from EGL wl_buffers.
- gles2: bind the display in wlr_renderer_init_wl_display() (the EGL
  implementation then provides its own wl_drm, so ours is skipped);
  WLR_EGL_NO_BIND_DISPLAY=1 turns it off.
- A wlr_buffer type for EGL wl_buffers, tried after all other buffer
  types (fallback resource interface), so that eglQueryWaylandBufferWL
  only sees buffers no other implementation claims (Weston's order).
- GLES2 textures from those buffers: one EGL image per buffer, re-bound
  on each commit like DMA-BUF textures (and like Weston), with a
  vertical flip for buffers whose origin is at the bottom left.
---
